        "question": "How do I set up VPN on my Mac?",
        "request_id": "1276d304-43cd-4607-a8e0-78c86349e303",
        "elapsed_s": 2.6276,
        "result": {
          "answer": "1. Open App Hub from Launchpad and install SecureTunnel. 2. When macOS asks, open System Settings, Privacy and Security, and allow the SecureTunnel system extension. 3. Allow SecureTunnel to add VPN configurations when prompted. 4. Click the SecureTunnel icon in the menu bar, choose Connect and sign in with LarkID. 5. Approve the prompt in LarkID Authenticator; the menu bar icon shows a closed lock when connected.",
          "citations": [
            {
              "chunk_id": "KB-1017:recursive:9b9ea2f835e2c40e:0",
              "document_id": "KB-1017",
              "source": "D:\\AI-Engineering\\servicedesk-copilot\\data\\kb\\KB-1017.html",
              "quote": "1. Open App Hub from Launchpad and install SecureTunnel. 2. When macOS asks, open System Settings, Privacy and Security, and allow the SecureTunnel system extension. 3. Allow SecureTunnel to add VPN configurations when prompted. 4. Click the SecureTunnel icon in the menu bar, choose Connect and sign in with LarkID. 5. Approve the prompt in LarkID Authenticator; the menu bar icon shows a closed lock when connected."
            }
          ],
