      {
        "question": "How do I fix Windows VPN error 809?",
        "request_id": "b829d73a-d13f-4a50-95ca-9f7ccc130a44",
        "elapsed_s": 2.2094,
        "result": {
          "answer": "1. Connect the laptop to a phone hotspot and try the VPN. If it works, the first network is blocking it. 2. Restart the home router, then try again. 3. In the router settings turn on IPsec passthrough, sometimes called VPN passthrough. 4. In SecureTunnel open Settings, Protocol, and choose TLS fallback, which uses TCP port 443. 5. Restart the laptop and connect again. 6. If error 809 appears on every network, raise a ticket for Network Operations and attach the SecureTunnel log bundle.",
          "citations": [
            {
              "chunk_id": "KB-1018:recursive:31cdc78bfbe98fa2:0",
              "document_id": "KB-1018",
              "source": "D:\\AI-Engineering\\servicedesk-copilot\\data\\kb\\KB-1018.md",
              "quote": "1. Connect the laptop to a phone hotspot and try the VPN. If it works, the first network is blocking it. 2. Restart the home router, then try again. 3. In the router settings turn on IPsec passthrough, sometimes called VPN passthrough. 4. In SecureTunnel open Settings, Protocol, and choose TLS fallback, which uses TCP port 443. 5. Restart the laptop and connect again. 6. If error 809 appears on every network, raise a ticket for Network Operations and attach the SecureTunnel log bundle."
            }
